  "document": {
    "abstract": "This specification defines WebVTT, the Web Video Text Tracks format. Its main use is for marking up external text track resources in connection with the HTML <track> element. WebVTT files provide captions or subtitles for video content, and also text video descriptions [MAUR], chapters for content navigation, and more generally any form of metadata that is time-aligned with audio or video content.\nThis specification is based on the Draft Community Group Report of the Web Media Text Tracks Community Group.",
